      "reasons": [
        "The definition claims “fast-progressing” behavior, but the packet does not explicitly describe speed of progression—only that survival decreases with increasing tumor grade and that patients often experience recurrence.",
        "The definition states that the tumor has a “greater tendency to worsen”; the packet supports recurrence and poorer prognosis with higher tumor grade, but does not explicitly support the specific phrasing of a “greater tendency to worsen.”",
        "Most other elements are broadly consistent (worse survival with higher grade; grade IV glioblastoma has poor prognosis due to “aggressive character”), but the unsupported “fast-progressing” component is substantive."
